---
import { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';
const base = '/participation-age-cohort-scenarios/20261107-01/';
type Range = { lower: number; upper: number } | null;
type Estimate = { subset: number; prior_choice: string;
	birth_year_only_hypothetical_original_cohort: Range;
	estimated_current_reported_prior_count: number;
	reported_opposite_choice_count: number | null;
	birth_year_only_original_coalition_scaled_switching_pct: Range;
	birth_year_only_apparent_absence: Range; marginal_sensitivity_apparent_absence: Range;
	historical_certain_group_raw_n: number; historical_certain_group_effective_n: number };
const review: { estimates: Estimate[] } = JSON.parse(readFileSync(`public${base}summary.json`, 'utf8'));
const ages: Record<number, string> = { 53: '18-29', 54: '18-44', 55: '65+' };
const count = (value: number | null) => value === null ? 'Unavailable'
	: (Math.round(value / 1000) * 1000).toLocaleString('en-US');
const range = (value: Range) => value === null ? 'Unavailable' : `${count(value.lower)} to ${count(value.upper)}`;
const rate = (value: Range) => value === null ? 'Unavailable'
	: `${value.lower.toFixed(1)}% to ${value.upper.toFixed(1)}%`;
const prior = (value: string) => value === 'D' ? 'Harris to R' : 'Trump to D';
---

<section id="participation-age-scenarios" class="participation-current" aria-labelledby="age-scenarios-title">
	<header class="section-intro">
		<p class="kicker">Conditional national scenarios · 2024 coalitions, prospective 2026 ages</p>
		<h2 id="age-scenarios-title">Switching and apparent absence by age</h2>
		<p>These scenarios scale the official 2024 Harris and Trump coalitions using CES survey
			birth-year composition, then compare them with matched SSRS current-age House cross-tabs
			and UF preliminary 2026 ballot estimates. Both years cover the 50 states excluding D.C.
			This is not a linked panel of the same people.</p>
	</header>
	<p><strong>No measured staying-home rate is identified.</strong> The original group is a
		hypothetically aged 2024 coalition, not observed 2026 survivors or residents. Apparent absence
		is that hypothetical total minus estimated current participants reporting the same prior vote;
		it includes mortality, migration, recall and source-population error. Negative residuals are
		retained as source/model diagnostics, not physical nonvoting counts.</p>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Conditional national age-coalition reference scenarios">
		<table>
			<caption>Counts rounded to the nearest thousand for display. Birthday-only ranges vary
				calendar-year age ambiguity, not sampling or survival uncertainty. None is a confidence interval.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Prospective age</th><th scope="col">Reported switch</th>
				<th scope="col">Hypothetical original coalition</th><th scope="col">Current reported prior voters</th>
				<th scope="col">Reported opposite choice</th><th scope="col">Switching / original coalition</th>
				<th scope="col">Apparent absence: birthday-only</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{review.estimates.map(row => <tr data-age-coalition={`${row.subset}-${row.prior_choice}`}>
				<th scope="row">{ages[row.subset]}</th><td>{prior(row.prior_choice)}</td>
				<td>{range(row.birth_year_only_hypothetical_original_cohort)}</td>
				<td>{count(row.estimated_current_reported_prior_count)}</td>
				<td data-age-switchers>{count(row.reported_opposite_choice_count)}</td>
				<td>{rate(row.birth_year_only_original_coalition_scaled_switching_pct)}</td>
				<td data-age-birthday-absence>{range(row.birth_year_only_apparent_absence)}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p>The original-coalition denominator above differs from switching among current voters.
		SSRS choices can retain pre-election intentions. The calculation assumes the published
		group/prior-choice composition applies to the matching ballot-caster population, which
		has not been independently validated. Ages 18-29 and 18-44 overlap; do not add them.</p>
	<div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Historical age support and wider assumed sensitivity">
		<table>
			<caption>Historical bases cover the certain-age support only, not the boundary-year
				respondents. Effective n is a weight diagnostic, not a design-aware precision guarantee.</caption>
			<thead><tr><th scope="col">Prospective age</th><th scope="col">Prior vote</th>
				<th scope="col">Historical raw n</th><th scope="col">Historical effective n</th>
				<th scope="col">Apparent absence: wider assumed stress</th></tr></thead>
			<tbody>{review.estimates.map(row => <tr data-age-diagnostics={`${row.subset}-${row.prior_choice}`}>
				<th scope="row">{ages[row.subset]}</th><td>{row.prior_choice === 'D' ? 'Harris' : 'Trump'}</td>
				<td data-age-raw-base>{row.historical_certain_group_raw_n.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td>
				<td data-age-effective-base>{row.historical_certain_group_effective_n.toFixed(1)}</td>
				<td data-age-stress-absence>{range(row.marginal_sensitivity_apparent_absence)}</td>
			</tr>)}</tbody>
		</table>
	</div>
	<p><strong>Wider stress is not a confidence interval.</strong> Each coalition has 486 scenarios:
		two birthday endpoints, historical fractions shifted by -2/0/+2 percentage points, estimated
		ballots scaled by 95/100/105%, group and prior-share rounding by -0.5/0/+0.5 points, and
		balanced recalled-choice transfers by -2/0/+2 points. The main grid holds conditional choice
		fixed; a separate group/prior/choice rounding envelope is preserved in the download.
		These are assumed stresses, not exhaustive empirically estimated uncertainty. Marginal
		endpoints must not be added.</p>
	<details class="explorer-notes"><summary>Source matching, historical support and withheld quantities</summary>
		<p>CES uses validated 2024 participation, self-reported presidential choice and the documented
			post-election validated-voter weight. Unknown birth years remain in the coalition denominator;
			boundary-year birthdays are not imputed. Current SSRS age groups use their actual published
			population shares and joint recalled-choice/current-choice cells, never products of unrelated
			preference marginals. Suppressed choices remain unavailable. UF totals are initial estimates,
			not final counted ballots. The current electorate is not reweighted to the 2024 partisan split.</p>
		<p>Measured staying home, identified new/returning voters, demographic turnout rates, causal
			persuasion, shares of total swing and design confidence intervals remain unavailable.
			No state, county or precinct allocation is made. The complete package contains the six
			disclosure-reviewed broad historical supports, four selected current survey tables, full
			licensed UF inputs, official FEC workbook, exact code/tests, methods and all 2,916 scenarios;
			no personal records, small boundary cells or restricted NORC materials are included.</p>
	</details>
	<div class="download-links">
		<a href={`${base}complete-analysis.zip`} download>Complete age-scenario inputs + code + results (ZIP)</a>
		<a href={`${base}summary.json`} download>Age-scenario summary + qualifications (JSON)</a>
		<a href={`${base}download.json`} download>Age-scenario archive bytes and SHA-256</a>
	</div>
</section>

<style>
	#participation-age-scenarios { min-width: 0; margin-block: 1.5rem 2rem; }
</style>
